.TH GITEA-PRUNE-ORPHANS.SH 1 "2026-04-25" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitea-prune-orphans.sh \- remove Gitea mirror repositories no longer present on configured GitHub users
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash gitea-prune-orphans.sh
.RI [ --dry ]
.RI [ config.json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitea-prune-orphans.sh
scans mirror repositories in the configured Gitea user account, checks whether each repository exists under any configured GitHub user, and deletes mirrors that no longer exist upstream.
.PP
Only repositories identified as mirrors are considered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry
Preview mode. Print mirrors that would be deleted without performing deletion.
.TP
.I config.json
Optional path to configuration file. If omitted, defaults to
.B config.json
in the script directory.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The script reads these keys from the config file:
.TP
.B GITEA_URL
Base URL of the Gitea instance.
.TP
.B GITEA_USER
Owner account in Gitea to scan.
.TP
.B GITEA_TOKEN
Gitea API token with repository delete permission.
.TP
.B GH_USERS
Array of GitHub users/organizations used for orphan checks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on completion. Returns 2 for missing prerequisites or invalid configuration. Returns 3 for repository-list API failures.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview deletions only:
.PP
.B bash gitea-prune-orphans.sh --dry
.PP
Delete orphan mirrors using explicit config path:
.PP
.B bash gitea-prune-orphans.sh ./config.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gitea-sync-all.sh (1),
.BR git-mirror.sh (1)
